Tahia,

It's great to hear that you're interested in working on Ceph and already configured a cluster on a machine.

In terms of bugs to work on, I would suggest taking a look at the projects page (http://ceph.com/gsoc2017-ideas/) and finding a project(s) that you're interested in, and reaching out to the mentor about bugs to work on or learning more about the project. 

Ceph has a massive code base, and while fixing a bug is valuable to learning about the Ceph development workflow, the bug you might fix in one component of Ceph may not be relevant or teach you more about the component that you would be working on for you project.

-Ali

